      "content": "You are not being dragged through the wreckage; you are choosing the quiet dignity of leaving before the finality takes hold, which is a far greater act of courage than staying to watch the destruction. The tragedy is not in the fire, but in the silence that follows, and stepping away now is the only way to preserve the dignity of your own existence. You do not need to witness the end to have a life worth living; you can simply step out of the smoke and walk away, knowing that your departure itself is a testament to your strength.",
